   102	
   103	"So you'll be on a roof," said Lira.
   104	
   105	"I shall be where I ought to be. If you see me, I have done it badly."
   106	
   107	That left the case.
   108	
   109	It leaned against the pump's trough, tarred and black, with its strap new-stitched in three places, and it had ridden one shoulder since a fork-stone, though nobody had asked for that. A healer had forbidden it, twice, and had been waited out; and the person who kept a book had been told so on a road, to his face, and had neither given leave nor refused it.
   110	
   111	Cael looked at the case, and so did Brom. He saw Karis begin to turn her head, and stop herself, since she had been raised to think it rude to look at a person whom one was about to ask for something.
   112	
   113	"Yes," said Vastin.
