   168	
   169	"Habit."
   170	
   171	"Out here the habit's the tell."
   172	
   173	He let that lie for the length of a breath. He was not looking at the man. He was looking at the hand that hung in the air, as he had looked at it three times that morning and said nothing.
   174	
