   193	"What's there?" said Lira. She said it without any mischief.
   194	
   195	"A courier's flat, strapped. A calfskin, with four stones on it." He was a long time over each. "A book that belonged to a dead man. An iron stake that has never been driven. Some pebbles, which that young woman has laid out by size." He stopped. "And a wind. I had not noticed until now that there was a wind."
