   236	
   237	Gault had signed a figure for him every week for two years, to the decimal, and had ended by writing that no instrument would have such a thing to measure again. Pike had one arm and a horn ink-pot, and had never owned an instrument in his life. Somebody had told him that some were lying at a place, and that a crew had gone to look; and he had put down that they were not there, and that the crew was. Cael thought that he would have liked to see the two men at one table.
