editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:10:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:14:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 3 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Deployment since the Line is thirty-two** at the end of Movement 3 (one Ember grain and one Wind burst away, both at the cut on the 279th). Ten fragments; the eleventh has not come; nothing came of standing two feet from Vastin's wall. Purse 138 marks. (2) **Iron Wall has been shown once** (the cut): a plane from a line struck with the stick, wall to wall, rooted — he may not lift a foot — loud to anything that hunts a Path, and it spent him to the floor. **Vastin's RIGHT knee** was bitten there; Oryn shut the holes and bound the joint with laths for a month from the 279th (stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall); he said "I cannot undertake" and has kept it to the letter. Brom's right foot, two toes, ten days from the 279th. (3) **The date:** Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. No figures are ever printed, no span of years is computed, and there is **no second calendar or offset** (one registry reckoning only). Vastin does no date arithmetic and knows nothing of it. (4) **The records at the spring:** Karis has matched FOUR sign-groups to the hide and has given NO number of places; no fifth place has been described. The same stroke and bar stands in a ruled square on all four matched places' sheets (in the field: stake thirty-two and the fourth site's thirty-fours only). The remark "Behaves as device. Cannot be." is on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; its hand is NOT identified. The instruments column reads true on every line. (5) **Seln has taught one thing, to Vastin** ("Draft nothing. Just look."). Cleon has been named (by Karis) and nothing more is known of him than her protected lines give. (6) **Oryn** went north from the fork on the 281st with the brown mule, her linen and her crossbow with one bolt; Millrace in three weeks; she owes Cael the reading ("the one thing I'm walking up that road owing"); the station term is written in the log. Her past as told at the fork: a house for the sick in a city inside the Line, the column for the patient's tier, a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; she has not been through a gate since. (7) **Loads:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; the tarred kit case on Vastin, taken up unasked at the fork-stone; Karis the flat and the hide, with the copied page in oilcloth in her coat. **Cael laid his hand on that page once, on the rise.** Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise. (8) **Stillhounds:** a den that has learned a road runs to where a declaration ends (Karis's sixth line). The sixty yards of four-strand rope are still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:16:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 1]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:21:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 19–22; §3 A (the alley), B 3–4; §5 (the Seln and Karis cutaways); §7.1 (Iron Wall, Rune Path); §8 (the alley); §10 (Tier A 9, 12; S10–S12 lines); §12 C2; §13.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:26:It is the 284th day, under Treswick. The lamp goes into the middle gallery. A light is already on at its end, and a man is already reading.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:30:This is the archive's first week. Karis has found the room she has wanted all her life. A marshal learns his name is a blade with no handle. A craftsman shows how he reads a made thing's bones. Brom is offered the life his family wanted and picks up a box. Seln looks at the door his old trade would have used and decides nothing. Then the faction reaches inside the walls. A man with nothing behind him holds a line for people the Compact would restrict, and Cael comes away with the eleventh. We cross the first third into the middle, and progression language surfaces at the turning points: Rune explained, Iron Wall paid, the notice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:33:- **The Deepstacks (284th).** The galleries, the shelving, the smell of a place where nothing has been decided. Cleon reads to the end of his page first. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." Cleon: "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael finds himself, for the first time, unfiled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:34:- **The yard door (285th).** Vastin's reflex: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —". **Seln answers truthfully** (ruling 25): "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." The narration records that Seln did not lie and what not lying cost him. "I'm sorry." / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." Cael's fellow-feeling on the landing. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:37:  - Cleon's board against the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit, verbatim.** "Same make."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:42:- **Seln's night walk.** Cael hears the room change shape. From a roof below the walls Seln looks at the registry and the station's light. "I looked at it." It is six words in the morning log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:43:- **Cleon's close (287th), verbatim:** "documentation … built the same way twice … never once slept well since."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:44:- **The alley (290th dusk; ~4,000, developed).** Staging follows BOOK_MAP §8. Vastin turns uphill and roots the cut wall to wall: "there is no round." Nobody declares. Brom with a loose step-stone. Lira's drop, the knife into the stave's shaft. Cael stands still at the plane's foot for a minute and some, as "the reason". Seln's weighted cord from the roof takes the signaller. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave: none taken, no faces, nobody dead.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:48:**Cutaways (~4,500):** Seln, ~2,000, on the night walk: the roof, the locked case's weight [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 23], the registry's door, deciding nothing. **The contents stay unknown.** Karis, ~2,500, in the decipherment: her method, her refusal to guess, the letters coming one by one. **The leaf is not readable in this movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:49:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Brom 2, Seln 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Lira 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:51:## What must remain true / withheld
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:53:- Cleon's Path is shown from outside only. The *inside* (the lean) and the acquisition belong to Movement 6. **No twelfth here.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:55:- Karis does not read the leaf yet. The bundle is on Cleon's shelf, a thing with a lean and no language.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:66:The faction knows where they sleep, and they know the crew knows it. A man who held a wall for them has asked for it to be entered, and Cael has entered more than the man knows. Karis has three days left of Cleon's week. A board leans, and a boy holding a lamp has started to notice which way.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:1:# Movement brief 004 — Inside Walls
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:8:- Owner names: no new names. The clerk stays unnamed ("do not name"). No new hold names on Oryn's route; use Oxhollow or none.
