editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18:> Movement 4 already carries day 281, six people/no mule, boxes on Brom/Lira/Cael, kit case on Vastin, the road posts, the inward reads, the station promise, and no new fragment (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,31–33,43–46`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving details:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:20:> - **Paper custody:** Karis has the flat under one arm and the hide under the other; inside the flat are six counted/re-taped rows with the original technician's sheet restored to the end of row two, plus the completion report and her copy; Vastin's copied page remains in its oilcloth inside her coat; Cael laid his hand on it once, on the rise, and gave it back (coordinator ruling: the author's beat is kept) (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:141–149,155–157`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:207,271–291`). Karis also has the dead surveyor's ledger/notebook; Seln's case remains shut on his own strap (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:183–187`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:39–41`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:21:> - **Knowledge:** Cael and Seln alone know that the unprinted date matches Cael's Kindling day; neither has said or written it, neither has interpreted the sequence, and neither knows for certain what the other concluded (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3–31,59–65,85–149`). Karis knows both men have read the sheet but not what they made of it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:143–149`). Vastin heard the records reading but does not know the arithmetic, integration mechanism or Cael's fragments (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`). Oryn heard the archive discussion from the basin but not the date conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:229–231`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:22:> - **Bodies:** Vastin's right knee is shut, lath-bound and on day two of Oryn's thirty-day month on the 281st; stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall, and he has finally accepted being priced equally (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:151–169`). Brom's right two toes are bound with eight days left on the ten-day term, and his right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot; he must put a load down if it speaks (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:75`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:131–139`). Lira's arm remains slow and is on day sixteen out of wool (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:119–129`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:> - **Money/objects:** purse 138; reserve sealed; sixty yards of four-strand still owed; Pike's thumbed slip is in Brom's shirt; no cordage was bought (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:149–165`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101,187`). Oryn's empty bowl is Brom's to carry (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:221–223`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:26:> - **Treswick/day:** it is a little before noon on day 281, at the top of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. The six have seen a bluff, river loops, three tiered walls and the pale steady station light; Cael turned his eyes to the lowest wall, and Lira has not yet performed the packet's unasked matching discipline (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:233–269`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,43`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:28:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 1]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:38:It is the 281st day, on the border road's last stretch. The city grows by the wayposts: nine miles, six, three. There are six of them and no mule. The boxes are on Brom's good shoulder, on Lira and on Cael, and the kit's case is on Vastin, who picked it up at the fork-stone unasked. Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:42:This is the book's one partly quiet movement. The reason: its tension is legal and bodily, a [SHATTERED] body entering a Compact city whose top holds a station. It does not need a fight. It holds a learning encounter in which an instrument fails, a confession, the city shown as a machine, and the irony that the only legal door into the oldest record of what Cael is admits him as a number. Progression teaching stays dense in the first third: the ten as currents, the Path-tiered city (passes, tier gates, the smith's two forges), and the provision's columns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:45:- **The reading inward (281st, the six-mile post).** First he works out the line between "stop touching it" and "do not read yourself". Then come the fourth and fifth readings. The ten are named as currents. The still place is read *around*, not touched. **Finding: the reading feels current; the still place has none; "a cord on a stone."** He needs an instrument for what does not move. He writes down later that he is afraid of that.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:46:- **Cael and Vastin on the road's edge.** Vastin sits, for the first time since the cut. "I read your file …" (the span anchored, not numbered: §12 C2). "You were the instrument." / "I was the error." **The confession, as narrowed:** "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." In return Cael gives him the instrument's nothing, the thing nobody else holds. It is not friendship. It is ground. Then **the log, verbatim** ("color" stands).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:47:- **Treswick (282nd).** The grey bridge is older than the walls. The outer gate counts heads and asks for nothing. The outer district works as a mechanism. The mule at the trough. The inn with two doors: 136. Each of them looks at the city in their own way. Vastin: "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once." Brom: "They shoe by the tier." Cael walks the district's edge. **The road to the registry crosses the square**, and the promise holds. **Seln's report:** the quarry, the provision, hands entered by count, the clerk, the exposure. "Four hands." / "I've two." "Entered by count. That's the door." **The close, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:48:- **Cleon at noon (283rd).** "Off floors." / "Fifty-two sheets." His terms. He stops a step late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:49:- **The provision (284th).** They go up by count under Cleon's pass, which the keepers count with a pen. The square is avoided by Seln's route. Four hands: Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin, who says "Yes" before anyone can ask. Seln is not on the count. The clerk does not ask, and writes "four". **Lira's ladder does not pull.** The iron door. "The tiers closed, and the dark opened."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:52:**Cutaways (~4,000):** Oryn, ~2,500, on her north circuit: Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, the unread ribs on her mind. Vastin, ~1,500, in the outer district inn ("the first honest district"). He knows nothing of the mechanism and does no date arithmetic.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:53:**Development:** about 15 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 2–3, Lira 2, Seln 1–2, Karis 1–2, Brom 1, Oryn 2, Cleon 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:55:## What must remain true / withheld
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:57:- Cael never sets foot on the square or the station steps, and does not look at the crown. Lira keeps the same discipline unasked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:59:- Cleon's Path and tier come through Seln's report ("Rune Path. Bronze.": ruling 17). Cleon takes no notice of Cael. Cleon's Path is **not shown** in this movement. Bones come in Movement 5.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:66:Treswick's texture: brokers' tally boards, the rope-walk, the ferry landing, the smith's two forges and the coloured coats at the gates. Which way Cael walks the district's edge. Whether the optional physical beat happens and what it is. How the counter talk about strata goes, heard through the yard door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:70:Cael is through an iron door older than the walls, as a hand carrying a box, into a dark that had been there before any of it was. Above him a whole city reads bodies. Below him nothing reads anything. He has a question he has never let anyone hold, and he is about to watch a stranger whose craft is reading how things are built.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen; no birthday this book. Ribs quiet since day 129. His Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark. He has no Path. Ten fragments at rest; the still place untouched since Oryn's order. **Birthday rule:** never place either birthday beside a season name, month order or count back (OWNER-pending #42/#48). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:17:| Seln | Shadow; Bronze; fifteen years' service. Fit. Locked case carried shut for twelve years and unopened; the protected six-year line is not the case's age. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:18:| Oryn | Tide; Iron R4 provisional. Last located at Thornwater, with route work north next; grey jenny and thirty-foot three-strand rope with her. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:28:**Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:38:**Seln knows:** the faction's craft, the completion report went west, the rival clock, the dead surveyor's paper and the fourth site's outside survey. His case remains unopened and undecided.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:48:**He does not know:** that the index is a grade; the Architect; Treswick's archive or Cleon; anything Vastin carries; that instruments will read wrong in his hands. The last is discovered on the 168th (Book 7 ends with the instruments reading TRUE in his hand; Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:62:- **Seln:** locked case, shut and unopened.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:76:| 6 | Shadow-adjacent | Seln | Idle cost from waking; used exactly twice (Ring, Stair); Stair bill dead to elbows; seal held and is shut at entry. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 16] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:92:| Seln | Says a thing once. Watches the rival clock. Gave the kit's ledger to Karis on the road and did not ask for it back. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:93:| Oryn | Terms of service; a route she owns. Cael's three readings and full telling are paid. Her withheld answer was never a debt and still stands. Her rule is in her hand and his. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 17] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:125:- **The stroke and bar** is on stakes thirty-two and thirty-four only. Karis cannot read the index and does not know it is a grade.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:128:- **"West" was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th**, in Karis's protected speech (Treswick, the last Compact city on the Line; the registry office on the old town; the Deepstacks under it). Cleon is not named. The protected closing log is on the 270th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:129:- **Lowmarch's cold term:** Pike's rate and "Eleventh" (said by Pike, to the keeper's "Pike,"); the axe-head hold's fence worked; the silent yard with Teague's crew (learning bouts, no wall drilled, no Force shown in Cael's presence); the ice road on the 161st; Seln's notched wand (the first notch is day 131).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:134:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial, cold read, source-distance (4 tracked passages, no dense scene; probe 1% / 4%), plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — fourteen applied by the coordinator, including the four protected units the author had left as markers and the cord's length). The audit also settled five conflicts between Book 8's plan and the locked Book 7 (the spear; Teague reading; Lira's asking; the stroke and bar; the cord), all resolved in the plan, not in Book 7. Same-author repair r1 in progress when this block was written; the CLOSED note follows when the recheck returns.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:137:- **Lowmarch in the cold (flag).** The ferryman's round shed has reed hurdles tied between its posts for the cold; its horse-walk is eight strides across; there is a stone trough inside the door, a mounting block, and a lean-to **rope-house** against it where he keeps his blocks and cordage. The hauling rope lies coiled against the drum. He has watched the river for "twenty cold terms". His ice: the shelf, then a skin that takes the snow, then "one night it goes blue"; it went blue on the 153rd night; he sounds it with an iron bar and marks his track with a double row of spruce boughs ("my green"), which swings wide at the bend above the landing, where a side water comes in under the western bank and the ice never shuts sound. He pulled the green on the 224th. Open water down the middle on the 230th. He has the scow on blocks before the 263rd and begins to knock them out on the night of the 270th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:138:- **What four a month buys (flag):** the hearth's end; the pot at dusk, a bowl a head; and the crew's names said to anybody who comes asking. Not bread, candles, the back room or the mule. "A cold term's five by my book": twenty, in front. The keeper comes out to his own door, behind the plank, to hear his floor priced (the join for the restored `The keeper said, "Pike," and Pike said, "Eleventh."`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:140:- **The cold-term board:** *Roof, the ferryman's rope-house; shingles found; five, when it has kept a thaw out.* · *The well-house at the south fork; a door hung and a hearthstone laid; three, and flour.* · the fence at forty. The five take the roof (five strokes). The roof is paid on the 268th and Pike says its line twice: **eleven lines** in his book at the movement's end.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:143:- **The silent yard (flag):** a square trodden under the ash, twelve strides on a side, a hazel peg at each corner, a bench from the upper inn on its western edge. Teague's rules: three touches; "a touch is what the one who took it calls"; over the pegs is a touch; nobody strikes what a healer has had her hands on this season. The name is the three grey men's. Bouts on the 148th (three to none) and the 158th (three to one); a sack game on the 190th, three a side.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:147:- **The ice road (flag):** a four-wheeled cart behind two mules, eighty yards out, with a dozen barrels and two pigs of iron for the smith; the carter heavy and grey-bearded, unnamed; one barrel of fish lost. Hauled out on the ferry's own rope and drum by Oryn's brown mule. Pike: "That's said. It's not entered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:151:- **Her case, as said on the 268th (flag; the place itself is now given only in her restored protected speech):** mine are the two steps before it: "I think that they are instructions." (the same forty-one kinds in the same order on three floors; a line that carries the circle's own measure), and that a key to the index exists and "is kept". The hide lies on Seln's oilcloth with the brass along its pencil line. Then the coordinator's three joins and the protected speech, in which **"west", "Treswick" and "the Deepstacks" are said aloud for the first time**. My earlier description of the archive, of the provision and of Karis's certificate is gone. **After the speech, mine:** Seln adds only what the speech does not have (a gate with a book in it; a station on its crown; the paper that executes "on the hour when any of us shows a certificate inside the Line"; one file not shut); Lira's certificate ("Iron, Rank One, with a seal on it"); Cael's "A registry's where they file you"; no ruling. The scene closes on "her first two words", which none of the six had ever said aloud as a place to go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:152:- **Seln's wand (repair r1):** one notch each morning from the 131st, the day after the clerk's packet went over on the 130th: eighteen on the 148th (the first bout, now headed with its day), twenty-eight on the 158th, the hundredth on the 230th; a second wand at forty on the 270th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:160:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventieth day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 131, 133, 138–146 (the fence; the herd on the 140th), 147, 148, 150, 158, 161, 168, 170 (Karis), 176, 190, 224, 230, 263, 264–265 (the saddle; the ford), 265–266 (Thornwater), 267–268 (down), 268, 270. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page. The river: shelf ice on the 131st; a road from the 154th; open at the middle on the 230th; "a week" from carrying a boat on the 268th; the scow's blocks being knocked out on the night of the 270th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:162:**Where everyone is.** Six at the lower inn: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, and Oryn, who came down from Thornwater unasked because Lowmarch is her first stop after a thaw and the mill her second. Her brown mule is in the ferryman's shed. The mill's grey jenny is not mentioned after Book 7. Teague's five are at the upper inn; they do not appear after the 190th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:164:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-nine** (twenty-seven at entry; the read on frozen ground at the calf, the 140th; the read on river ice, the 161st). All ten tried in the cold term and written up as *The ten, by use*: Wind (the lock cannot be shortened, only placed), Ember (the burn), Shadow (held, not opened), Compression (both heels; ground worth a load), Pressure (seen coming; narrow and deep; comes back), Blade (short; the steel pays), the read (ground or air; a pace and a half; the eyes), Storm (one lane; ten counts; a fourth untried), Anchor (a point held to thirty; ten, twelve and fourteen feet), Tide (asked of Lira; told no; not used). Shadow used twice in all and shut. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else. **The still place** has not been read or touched. **The instruments:** on the 168th the kit's cord (four knots to a length) measured the inn yard at forty-two strides for Karis, Lira, Brom and Seln and at forty-one and a piece for him, three times; the Ternhall brass read a hair short in his hand and Hesk's a hair long; he has touched none of the three since; his ruling is *hold*; Oryn has been told and has no answer. Nobody has offered a cause. He lost to Teague's spear three to none (148th) and three to one (158th). He has entered Teague as the better captain. He has not ruled on Karis's case. He has written *West, and inside*. Body: sound; knuckles skinned on the 140th; near sight lost for an hour on the 140th and for an evening on the 161st, and back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:170:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **She has made her case to six** (the 268th): instructions; an index with a key that is kept; and then, in her protected speech, west, Treswick, the registry office on the old town, the Deepstacks under it, the old scholars' provision for a registered historical-studies practitioner, which she is not, and "a man there who is" (unnamed). She said the sentence whole to Cael on the 263rd, without the word west. She cannot read the four signs and has put no meaning on the stroke and the bar. She knows how the kit's cord is used and has taught the five. She has entered the anomaly as *Cause: not found. No inference entered.* and has written no sentence joining it to anything. Fifty-two sheets; the hide; the kit; the dead man's ledger, open now; a hair in her notebook. She keeps the purse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:172:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He kept the door at every trial with his back turned. He told only Brom about two posts. He counts the days since the clerk's packet went over on the 130th, a notch a morning from the 131st: eighteen on the 148th, twenty-eight on the 158th, a hundred on the 230th, and forty more on a second wand by the 270th. He watched the fire "as if he knew the road she meant" when Karis laid her palm where the bearing leaves the hide. He has taught nobody anything. **The case is on him, shut.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:174:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. She released the arm only when Lira took it; mended the ankle; answered Lira's thanks with "Route's whole… The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."; left the shoulder to the woman who tied it. She has seen the map with four rings and the line ("That's a line.") and has been told of the fourth site: twice the size, fenced, unentered. She has been told of the cord and the edges. **She has not read Cael** and has said that she will know what she is reading for before she does. At the word *station* she shut her mouth on a sentence and said nothing. She did not sit in the sixth place. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:176:**Teague and his crew.** He proposed and ran the silent yard to make his people better at fighting with no Path. He sent the young one to learn from Lira. His wrist is bound shut till the thaw on the older healer's order. His term stands. He knows nothing of the mechanism; he has seen a light in the shed and a guard at its door, heard a Wind's crack on two nights, and watched a pair of boots refuse something three times. The tall one, the bow and the older healer have said nothing to the five. Nobody in his crew is named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:180:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand** (96 − 20 for the cold stay; + 40 for the fence; + 5 for the roof; − 3 for the mule's shed). The reserve sealed and unopened. Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman, wanted with the first boat; one reed hurdle; a letter to Ephram. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. Both brass edges are in their cloths.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:186:**Words said aloud for the first time.** *West* (as the place to go), *Treswick* and *the Deepstacks*: all three by Karis, in her protected speech at the board on the 268th, and by nobody before it. Cael writes *West, and inside* on the 270th. Not said at all: Cleon's name; Vastin's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:188:**Open threads.** A ruling that Cael has put off until daylight. A ferry that runs in a week, and whatever a desk has had a hundred and forty days to send over on it. A provision that nobody has seen used. A sentence that a healer swallowed. A cord that reads short in one hand. Four signs and a mark. A shoulder in another woman's knot. An arm that is slow. A captain's term. A rope, a hurdle and a letter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:196:- **Lira:** her right ankle is newly mended; she walks on the ball of it and wears the oversized carter boot without its old stuffing. Her left arm is released but slow for a month, aches in wet for a year, and is not to be fallen on (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127-151`). She still has Oryn's crossbow, hook, and one bolt; no return occurs (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:7`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:283`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:198:- **Karis:** fifty-two sheets, map, two straightedges, kit, opened field ledger, one stored hair, and the eleven-line case remain under her control. She cannot read the four-sign index or know it is a grade; she has entered no causal theory (`manuscript/chapter-04.md:253-281`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:145-195`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:227-253`). After fix 14, *west* has now been spoken once at the day-268 table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:199:- **Seln:** his locked case remains shut; he taught nobody; he has begun a second hazel wand and reaches forty notches on day 270; he already recognized Treswick/Deepstacks when Karis said them (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:247,253,283`). He still does not explain the rival clock.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:202:- **Money, board, debts, and letters:** 118 living marks; sealed reserve untouched; eleven completed Pike lines; cloth still eleventh; sixty yards of four-strand rope owed for the first boat; one reed hurdle owed; Ephram's letter still due on the first boat; mule's cold-term shed fee paid (`manuscript/chapter-01.md:271`; `manuscript/chapter-03.md:295-299`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:215-219,281-283`; `book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-91`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:205:**Movement 1 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Sol recheck of repair r1: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all four tracked passages RESOLVED against the source; no new tracking; every binding ruling above borne out by the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch3, the author's own "his Path" (of Teague) now reads "the Force"; ch6, Seln's sentence after Karis's protected speech now gives the asset-restriction as locked Book 6 ch58 states it — **the paper executes when an enrolled name is written in a book inside a district, and must be served within the hour** (not "a certificate inside the Line"). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report after the fixes. Final: 30,941 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (9 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment twenty-nine; day 270 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:214:- **What Vastin added about the layer is exactly four things:** it cannot be reached (there is no key); a citation to a designer; the suppressed survey records; the technician's line. The layer's existence was Karis's already (her protected line stands unglossed, OWNER-pending #48). Nothing says that menders, technicians or any office know more; nothing says it has been tried.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:215:- **The three papers.** (1) **The records:** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather; six taped rows, a year to a row, of survey abstracts measured in lengths, knots and strides, with the dead surveyor's four-sign index printed at their heads; an **anomaly column** in which every sheet, in every hand, for six years carries the one word *Total* (an entry, not a sum; no figure); "More than four" (Karis, counting distinct sign-groups; she gives no number); the Fallow completion report is the last, loose sheet, and carries **five strokes for a name and a count of six** (locked Book 7 ch40, ch43), not five names. (2) **The page:** a COPY in Vastin's own hand of one line from an old register, carried in oilcloth in his coat: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". "The Architect" is a title, not a name, and a word Karis has never met in any stratum. It is never called a leaf; **the leaf has not appeared**. (3) **The technician's sheet:** the two protected lines with a date between them, a brush bar across what followed, and Karis's *not read*. **The date is a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and is never printed as figures** (the source gives none; no owner decision is needed). The office had filed the sheet at the end of the second row and it lies there again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:216:- **Seln went still at the date** and said only "I have read it." He has not said the sum. Cael does not know what it was and has not read the date closely. **Nobody has connected the date to anyone**, and nobody has interpreted the sequence. "Classification event" is not defined.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:217:- **Speakers (protected):** "Archmarshal" is Cael's; "What follows you," is Lira's; "More than four." is Karis's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," is Oryn's (Karis owns the order to bed). The long table's close is verbatim. "Nothing that can cross the Line"; the rim of the Stair "is not mine".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:218:- **Karis's receipt** (unsealed, signed K.) is in Vastin's coat. Karis holds all three papers and her copy of the sheet. Seln's second wand (forty-seven notches, a hundred and forty-seven days) lies under the lamp; he will cut no more.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:226:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (1 tracked passage, ch12 scene 3; probe 2% / 12%, the excess being protected and plan-quoted document text); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR; 46 exact fixes, of which the coordinator applied 24 — protected units restored, two speakers corrected, "leaf" to "page" — and sent 22 to the author to recompose in voice). Coordinator rulings against the audit: the technician's date is NOT owner-pending (the source prints no value; the page shows a date and no figures); the completion report carries five strokes, not five names (Book 7 ch43:51), where the audit's fix kept "five names". **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:229:- **The ferry's rig (flag).** The scow hangs from the cable by two running blocks, one over her bow and one over her stern, each on **a strap of plaited hide as long as a man** to a post at her rail. In slack water she crosses "set a little aslant on her two straps, so that the current itself shouldered her along the cable"; the hauling rope from her bow turns through a block lashed to **an oak post at the landing's head** and so into the shed. The drum has **an iron dog** (a pawl) hinged to the shed's king-post. The ferryman had two hauling ropes "before the snow"; the second, sent across by a skiff when the first strands, is the sixty yards owed. The old slip's **sill** lies under the mud two strides south of the post. In flood the cable bellies to the south; she crossed light in three minutes and came home in twenty-two. The rope has "two yarns gone where she bore on the sheave". The new stern strap is rove out of the tail of the stern line. The fare is a copper a head.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:233:- **Seln's account of the gate (flag):** a man in the gate asks each person "for a name, and where the name is registered", and writes it; "every counter in every district keeps a list", read against each name as it is written; **the man who writes the name is the man who serves the paper.** What it holds: Lira's and Karis's certificates, kept for a slip, pending; Brom's Copper and the unsigned finding, "frozen as they stand"; and of Cael, "the thing that it holds is you… You would be produced", to a frame. Seln is not one of the four ("I was employed"). **Vastin, from the inside (ch11):** the instrument is drawn on the code's fourteenth chapter, ninth part; it does not wait upon a frame and does not lapse; he could not have lifted it when he held the seal; nothing lifts it "short of the settling of his status; and his status can be settled only on a plate."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:234:- **Oryn at Lowmarch (flag):** her bench is a form set along the wall under the eave, a yard past the right-hand post of Pike's plank, by the door of the keeper's wash-house, where she works with the door open. Nine on the first morning. She takes payment in kind. "I'll not spend on what grease will do." She does not go up the bank to the older healer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:237:- **The bout (flag):** the 273rd, in the silent yard's square; a stave a hand taller than Lira against Cael's short one; 2–3 to her. Her left hand comes a beat behind her right. The arm "told" her once, in the third exchange, at a square block. She fell beside it, not on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:240:- **What Vastin adds about the layer (repaired: four facts and no more).** (1) It cannot be reached: he asked to be shown what the office holds upon the thing beneath the function; "The office has one page upon the matter, and it is the office's own. The page says that the layer is not to be opened; and it gives as its reason that it cannot be"; it "reserves no leave to anybody". (2) The citation: in the oldest register of housings that he was let to see, the line for the layer has no maker's name but a word and a place. (3) The held records (the flat). (4) The technician's line. **Cut in repair:** the frame-shop mender, the shimmed frame, the rule of the shop, the office's schedules, and any history of attempts. He could not go to the archive himself: an archive on the Line keeps a book at its door. Brom and Lira say what it changes: "So there's nobody to ask"; "it'll not be the people who own the plates that tell him."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:241:- **The completion report (repaired to Book 7).** It carries the Fallow posting's head, a town on no registry map and a board; **"where a crew's name should have been there were five strokes, and after the strokes a count, which was six."** No names. It reached Vastin as a courtesy copy with no routing note; it took him the cold term to find the file that it belonged to, "which stands in no register". He does not know who had the abstracts held, and looked. Whether the copy was sent to him on purpose is Seln's question, left open.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:242:- **The flat (repaired):** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather, "as broad as a man's shoulders and no thicker than two fingers", stamped *BY SEAT COURIER. BY HAND.*; six rows, a year to a row, the newest uppermost, each in a tape; a pocket in the lid. **The abstracts:** printed forms; four signs and a number at the head (the Stair's sheet has the dead surveyor's four signs and thirty-two); a column for the day in the office's reckoning; a measure given in lengths, knots and strides; and a narrow right-hand column whose printed head says that it is for **the anomaly**. **In every clerk's hand, in every one of six years, that column holds the single word *Total*, and nobody has written a second word beside it.** There is no figure and no sum. Karis counts more than four different groups of signs in the newest row, on her fingers, and will not say a number until she has checked it in daylight. No sheets are counted.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:243:- **The page (repaired): a copy.** One sheet of the house's plain desk paper, folded twice, in Vastin's own square upright hand, in fresh ink. He copied the line "from a record that is older than the section it is filed in, in a room where I had the right to read and no right to copy", with the word and the place "exactly as they are written there, letter for letter", and the schedule of housings round it (a number, a date of setting and a mender's mark to each) to show where the line falls. He read the pages on both sides and did not copy them. **No cut edge, no blade, no inquiry, and no prompt from the ninth fragment.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:246:- **Names given at the board (ch10):** the six tell Vastin their names; he had Cael's and Karis's from paper and "took some trouble never to learn" the others. Seln gives his.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:252:**Where everyone is.** Seven under the lower inn's roof: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln; Oryn, who is on her road and at her bench by first light; and **Vastin, in the loft over the tap, at a copper a night**, who is on nobody's sheet and has asked for nothing but a bed. Teague's five are at the upper inn, with forty sacks of salt on the bank. The brown mule is in the ferryman's shed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:254:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: thirty** (the read on the ground at the landing, the 277th). Shadow used twice in all and shut; held at dusk on the 272nd and the 277th. Anchor's counted uses still two. Tide: Oryn twice, himself three times, nobody else; he did not ask to read the knee. **The still place** has not been read, touched or named. He has not touched the cord or either brass edge for a hundred and nine days; the ruling is *hold*. His near sight went at the landing and was back for print by the afternoon. **He has not ruled.** He will say it "at the plank in the morning, in daylight" and ask for hands. He has not touched the copied page; his hand lay a hand's width from it for the whole of a lamp. **He has not read the technician's date**: he was at the table's far end; he knows that it is a registry year and a day, and that it is the line at which Seln stopped; he chose not to go up the table and read it. He lost the bout to Lira, two touches to three. He has written to Ephram. He kept back his own question to Vastin (why the second reading was declined). He has told Vastin nothing of what he carries.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:262:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. He has spoken with Vastin for the first time (the doorway) and has given him his name. He has stopped his count at **forty-seven notches on the second wand (a hundred and forty-seven days)** and laid the wand on Karis's table. **He went still when Karis's pencil came to the date on the technician's sheet**, and said only "I have read it." He has taught nobody anything. He thinks the completion report may have been sent to Vastin on purpose and cannot tell. **The case is on him, shut.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:264:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. A bench under the eave since the 272nd. She saw the bout and said nothing. She has not asked about the knee, and Vastin has offered it to nobody; she seconded Karis's order to bed with one line about the stairs. **She has not read Cael.** She has shut her mouth three times on the same sentence. She did not sit on the stool. She does not know that Seln is Shadow's source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:272:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and eighteen marks in hand**, unchanged. The reserve sealed. Owed: **sixty yards of four-strand rope** to the ferryman (the cordage is on the western landing; his one hauling rope has two yarns gone). **The hurdle is paid.** **The letter to Ephram is sent.** The three boxes are at the hearth's end, roped. Stake thirty-two has still never been driven. On Karis's table: the flat (the sheet inside it), the broker's paper beside it, Seln's wand beside that, and the copied page at the far end.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:276:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before. The anomaly of the cord and the edges: the six. Karis's case: the six. What Vastin brought: the six and Vastin. Nobody has said who made the layer, or why, or what is running in it. Nobody has connected the sheet's date to anybody; only Seln has reacted to it, and only Cael has noticed that it was the date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:278:**Words said aloud for the first time.** *Vastin* (Seln, at the landing). *Treswick* by Vastin, at noon, from the other side. On paper only, and said by nobody: the title on the page. Not said aloud by anybody in chapters 10–12: *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:280:**Open threads.** A ruling to be given at the plank in the morning. A page that Cael has not touched. A date that stopped Seln and that Cael has not read. A bar with something under it. A count that Karis has not checked. A paper that came to a desk with no routing note. A sentence that a healer has swallowed three times. A knee that nobody has asked about. A man in a loft with a receipt and nothing to do. A rope on the wrong bank. A captain's term with no day in it. A question that Cael kept.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:283:Packet 003 already carries day 278, the clearance slip, Vastin at the door end and not on the sheet, the silent drill, the cut, the spring, the date sum, the fork and days 279–281 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:20–38`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:285:- **Paper custody and exact positions.** Karis holds the courier's flat, six taped rows, the completion report, Vastin's copied page, the technician's sheet, and her exact copy with the ruled box and *not read* (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:3–15,59–65,101–135,157–169`). At the close (as repaired), the flat and the completion report are under the lamp; the original technician's sheet lies back at the end of the second row, where the office had filed it, and Karis has noted its place beneath her copy; the copied page is on oilcloth at the bare far end. Vastin holds Karis's unsealed receipt inside the brown coat (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:157–175`). Seln's forty-seven-notch wand lies under the lamp beside the broker's sheet; he will cut no forty-eighth (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:251–255`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:286:- **What each knows.** All six and Vastin have heard no key, the citation/title/place, suppressed survey records and the technician's visible line/bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:149–193`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:201–257`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:59–151`). Karis has not finished the records and cannot read the index or bar (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:223–253`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:129–135,285–289`). Seln has done an unexplained sum and said only “I have read it”; Cael does not know the sum (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Vastin does not know the integration mechanism, directive, objection, what Cael carries, or what lies under the bar (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:129–131`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:119–129`). Nobody connects the date to anyone (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:137–153`). Oryn has not read Cael and has not asked to read Vastin's knee (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:29–47`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:288:- **Bodies and equipment.** Lira's arm will be on day 13 out of wool on day 278, still slow and wet-aching; her ankle is sound in the large boot (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127–151`; `manuscript/chapter-08.md:3–5,71–135,147`). Brom's right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:173–183`). The three boxes are roped tight for carrying with beckets out (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:243–249,281–283`). Seln's locked case remains shut (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:191–199`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:37`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:292:**Movement 2 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the 24 coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed; the page made a copy; the layer cut to four facts (Lira and Brom say what it changes: there is nobody to ask); *Total* made the anomaly column's entry; the technician's sheet read out by Lira with a date and no figures, filed at and laid back at the end of the second row; Seln's stillness re-entered in a new order; receipt and night log made literally true ("Read in part. Understood in no part."); the completion report's five strokes and count of six; ch7's opening oriented. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling above borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (ice 111 days; the wrist 124; the sling 170; the rim 163; the cord 109; the report 175). Three fixes applied by the coordinator: ch7 "a healer's Path" → "a healer's craft" (no possessive before Path in narration); ch8's bluff memory cut back to what Book 5 shows; ch10 "through a frame shop" removed. Rulings from the recheck: **Lira reading the sheet aloud is the author's staging and stands** (the map protects the wording, the sum and the withholding, not the reader); the two descriptions of the cited record agree. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 30,105 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (11 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; the night before day 278 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:295:## AFTER MOVEMENT 3 — chapters 13–19, days 278–281 (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:300:- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY-TWO**, both on the 279th at the cut: one grain of Ember at the mark (thirty-one; the heat came home along the left arm) and one Wind burst **away**, ten strides, to the north bank inside the wall (thirty-two). Pressure, Anchor, Edge, Storm and the read refused there. Shadow held, twice and sealed; Tide unused; no self-reading; Oryn has not read Cael. **Ten fragments: nothing came of standing two feet from the wall; the eleventh has not come.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:301:- **The cut (the author's staging stands; BOOK_MAP §8 allows it).** A hundred strides, a stride of ice down the middle, scree on the south, a low north bank, the sink fifty-five yards below it. Eight hounds (five seen, three hidden). The den had learned the road: it runs to where a declaration ENDS. Karis, Oryn and the mule were at the foot; Vastin, a stride behind Brom, stepped out and **declared Iron Wall** — a plane across the road from a line struck with his stick, wall to wall, two feet from Cael, rooted (he may not lift a foot), loud, spending him to the floor. Brom's rock (twice), Lira's knife with the left hand holding, Seln in the heap; five dead; **three went through the rotten ice of the sink and did not come up**. Costs: Brom's right foot (two toes, ten days from the 279th); **Vastin's right knee** (four holes shut by Oryn after "May I?" / "Yes"; the joint bound with laths; **a month** from the 279th: stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall). Karis's sixth line: *It goes to where a declaration ends, if it has learned that the declaring moves.* Twenty paid; **purse 138**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:302:- **Protected (speakers):** "Carters declare, on the ice." (the factor, unnamed, no pronoun); "It's clear because it's empty, not because it's safe," (Seln — the plan quotes only this clause; the source's fuller sentence contradicts the staging and was not restored); the wall lesson (Vastin) / "You do now," (Cael) / "I know fields…" (Vastin); the log verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:303:- **The spring (the 280th).** Six rows counted twice by two people. Five columns on every abstract: the day in the registry's reckoning; the station (eight points); the measure; *Instruments* ("Cord true. Edge true. Level true." on every line for six years); the anomaly (*Total*). **Karis matches FOUR sign-groups to the hide by their measures (three alike to the stride, one double) and gives no number of places; no fifth place is described** (held for the 298th). The measures have not changed in six years. The remark *Behaves as device. Cannot be.* stands in a ruled space on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; **its hand is not identified**; the space for remarks is gone from the next year's printing. **The grade:** a ruled square at the head of every sheet with the same stroke and bar on all four matched places, drawn no larger on the place whose measure is double; in the field it is on stake thirty-two and on the fourth site's thirty-fours only. Karis: a class, unread; "Two copies of one ignorance." Nobody says who set it or why. Karis stopped her lamps sentence with the ruler line and did not finish it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:304:- **The date.** Seln drew the technician's sheet from the foot of the second row; the row counted a sheet short in Cael's hands; Seln set the sheet before him without a word. **Cael read the date and knew it for the day of his own Kindling** (the first line of his file). Only Cael and Seln know; neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. Karis knows both have read the sheet. **No figures are printed, no span is computed, and there is NO second calendar** (the author's stations'-year offset was cut: the series calendar is the owner's). The sheet lies again at the foot of the second row.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:305:- **Vastin's three reflexes** (a directive; a classification; "This has to go up") and **the first thing Seln ever taught anyone:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." / "Draft nothing. Just look." **Cleon** was named for the first time (Vastin: "Treswick,"; Karis: "The archive under it. Cleon."; Cael: "Who's Cleon?"); OWNER-pending #52 verbatim, as Karis's own rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:306:- **The fork (the 280th evening; the 281st).** Oryn: "I'm not an archive person."; her past (a house for the sick in a city inside the Line; the column for the patient's tier; a woman from the river sheds whom she mended off the sheet; she walked out of a gate and has not been through one since — the author's, kept); "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second."; Seln's "Three weeks"; **the station term, written in the log and read back (verbatim)**; she priced all six, Vastin as long as the rest; "That's on me. It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." (the reading she has not given Cael); "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it."; "Not the steps," … "Not the square." She went north with the brown mule, her linen and the crossbow with its one bolt: five gates, the ford, Millrace in three weeks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:308:- **The rise (the 281st, near noon):** Treswick a day's walk off — a bluff in a river loop, three walls in tiers, a pale steady light on the crown that Cael does not look at. **Cael laid his hand on the page** (the author's; kept); it stays in its oilcloth in Karis's coat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:312:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (3 tracked passages, none dense; probe 2% / 15%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR; 102 exact fixes). Coordinator rulings against the audit, after checking the source and the locked Book 7: the cut's staging, the Ember use and the count of thirty-two KEPT (BOOK_MAP §8: private staging the author owns; the audit's 39 re-staging fixes declined); Oryn's past KEPT; Cael's touch of the page KEPT; the slip left as the packet quotes it; "every bar of a fence" KEPT (Book 7 ch58). Accepted from the audit: the six markers' speakers (two filled with the plan's own clause only); the loads for Movement 4; no fifth place or number; no second calendar; the remark's hand unidentified. Eleven fixes applied by the coordinator; the rest recomposed by the author. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:326:- **Iron Wall as shown.** Named by Vastin (16:109); **no tier is stated**. He steps into the road and brings the stick's foot down once; a line runs from his boots across the cut and cracks the ice white; "the air stood up from it": a face from bank to bank as tall as the scree, seen only by the frost that lies on it. It holds eight hounds at a run. It does not go anywhere; **he may not lift a foot**; each blow on it comes down through him into the stiff leg; it goes out of him steadily; it shuts the road and not the banks. "A Path of the tribunal floor… taught for fields; and a field is ground where a thing has been declared, a hearing, or a square, or a gate with a crowd at it." "I have stood on eleven such."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:327:- **The fight's count.** Brom's rock at the plane's south end; Lira, two-handed, on the hound at Vastin's knee; one broken on the plane in the second run; Seln's knife on one standing in the runnel; Brom's rock on the other. Three over the north bank and through the sink's ice. Seln was on the north bank above the sink when he said that the cut was clear because it was empty.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:329:- **Oryn's past (kept by the coordinator as written; the order of telling changed in r1).** "I'd my rank off a board at the foot of a bed." A house for the sick "inside a wall", forty beds, six healers; her Iron fourth rank is provisional because she "never stayed to have it confirmed". **A sheet on a board at each bed's foot: name, complaint, what had been spent, and a column for the patient's tier.** In a week of fever the spending went down the column from the top; a woman from the river sheds with no tier went to the bottom of the heap; Oryn went to her at night, off the sheet, and it was enough (**nobody died**); the woman who kept the house said that a healer who spends off the sheet has stolen from whoever stood next on it. Asked where, she will not say: "They keep the same sheet at the foot of every bed inside the Line." She walked out of a gate in the coat she stood in and has not been through one since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:331:- **The abstracts, read in daylight.** Karis counted every row twice and had each counted again; **no figure for any row is printed**. **She gives no number of places.** She sorted the sheets by their sign-groups, matched **four** to the hide by their measures (three alike to the stride, one double), and will not call the unmatched groups places until a sign can be read (17:27–39). **Five columns:** the day, in the registry's reckoning; the station (eight points); the measure; *Instruments*; and the anomaly. No radius of the four has changed by a stride in six years; four surveyors by their figures; three clerks' hands. The fourth column reads *Cord true. Edge true. Level true.* on every sheet. The three oldest rows have a ruled space at the foot headed *Remarks*, empty but once: **the Stair's sheet in the fourth row carries the protected four words, in a hand that is none of the three clerks'; Karis laid the dead man's ledger beside it and will not swear to the hand either way.** From the next year's printing the space is gone. Brom counts the three findings on his fingers (17:61, 17:77, 17:139).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:332:- **Seln's five omissions:** no routing head; no surveyor's name, a number in its place; nothing to say who ordered the survey; no column for a cause; the remarks space struck from the block after the year of the remark.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:334:- **The box.** To the right of the four signs and the number, on every abstract, a small printed square with a heading in the unread signs. **On all four of the hide's places it holds the short stroke and the bar, drawn alike**, the double-sized place included. "It is a class." Nobody says who filled it or by what rule. Nothing is said of any other sheet's square.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:335:- **The date.** The registry writes, on the first line of a person's file, after the name and before the bracketed word, the day on which the person was classed; every paper served on Cael began with it. Seln copied that line twice when he was employed at the house above Ostrand. The technician's sheet carries a registry year and a day in it, and it is that day. Seln knew it by the lamp, doubted a date read once over a shoulder in another person's pencil, and read the original a figure at a time in daylight. Cael laid the one date against the other, twice. **No figure, no span, no arithmetic owed to anybody; nothing spoken; nothing written.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:337:- **The loads from the fork (r1).** Boxes on Brom (left shoulder), Lira (both arms through the beckets) and Cael. Seln carries none: he goes ahead with his hands empty. **The tarred case was left leaning on the fork-stone; Karis stopped forty strides up; Vastin went back for it unasked, after Oryn was out of sight, hooked its strap with his stick without kneeling, and slung it above his sound leg.** He told Cael so at once: "I waited until she could not be put to the trouble of forbidding it a third time." "It is a cord, a mallet and one stake."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:338:- **Seln on the provision:** "A provision of that kind is granted by the week."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:345:**Calendar.** A little before noon on the **two hundred and eighty-first day past the Line**, going down the western side of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. Days on the page: 278, 279, 280, 281. No season, month or weekday name; no figures for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:347:**Where everyone is.** Six going down off the rise: Seln in front, Lira, Brom, Karis, and then **Cael with Vastin walking beside him on the ditch side** (from the top of the rise; nobody asked him to and nobody told him no). Oryn and the brown mule went north from the fork at first light and did not look back. Teague's five are east of the river.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:349:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments; no eleventh.** **Deployment thirty-two.** Left palm stung by Ember. He ruled on a job and has made no vow. **He has read the technician's date, laid it against the first line of his own file, and knows it for the day of his own Kindling. He has not written it, has told nobody, and has put no verb to it.** He said "You do now" to Vastin at the hold. He has written in the log, at Oryn's asking, that inside Treswick he does not go near the station. **He has laid his hand on the page once, on the rise, and Karis has it again.** He has seen the light on the crown and turned from it. He carries a box. He asked "Who's Cleon?" and has the name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:351:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Arm: the sixteenth day out of the wool on the 281st.** It held a hound by the scruff while the right hand struck; it votes; **she carries a box on her back with both arms through its beckets.** Oryn: slow for as long again; don't fall on it. **She no longer has the crossbow.** She knows that Cael has put something away and has not asked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:353:**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey at any point. Right shoulder still in the older healer's knot (if it tells him anything he is to put the load down and leave it down). **Right foot: two toes bruised, bound; ten days from the 279th, eight left on the 281st.** One box on the left shoulder. He has the purse and Pike's thumbed slip. He lays seven bowls and will carry Oryn's empty.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:355:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; one point set in the peats. She holds the flat (six rows, counted twice by two people and re-taped, the technician's sheet at the foot of the second), the completion report, the page in its oilcloth inside her coat, her copy, the hide, the kit's ledger and her notebook. She knows: four sign-groups matched to the hide and others matched to nothing, **no number given and none of the others called a place**; five columns; no measure changed in six years; the instruments true; the remark, and that she will not swear to its hand; the box, the same on all four; what an abstract is. She cannot read the index or the box. She began a sentence about lamps and stopped it with her rule, verbatim. She heard "I've read it" from Cael as she had from Seln and asked neither. She named the archive and Cleon. Six findings on her stillhound leaf.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:357:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. One hound with a short knife; "It's clear because it's empty, not because it's safe". **He has read the original date in daylight, has told nobody, and has set the sheet before Cael without a word; he does not know for certain that it was read.** He has taught for the first time ("Draft nothing. Just look.", to Vastin). **He carries no box.** **The case is on him, shut; no ruling upon it.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:359:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, provisional. On Pike's slip as its healer. She asked Vastin and had an explicit yes; shut four holes; bound the joint; two fingers on his wrist. She has priced all six and given Vastin as long as any. **She has not read Cael**: "It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." She has told the house, the column and why she left, and will not say where. She has her term in his log and has read it there. Gone north with the mule, her linen, and her crossbow with its one bolt; five gates, the ford, then Millrace in three weeks. She does not know that Vastin is carrying the kit's case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:361:**Vastin.** No office; **no age stated**. **Iron Wall declared once, on the 279th, in the cut**; spent to the floor. **Right knee: bitten, shut, bound stiff; the 281st is the second day of thirty**; on the stick; no kneeling, running or walls. He qualified every instruction. **He has not sat in front of the crew since the cut.** **He carries the tarred kit case (cord, mallet, stake thirty-two) on the shoulder above his sound leg, taken up unasked at the fork-stone after Oryn had gone, and has told Cael so.** **He walks beside Cael from the top of the rise.** He said the town's name at the spring, the first to say it since the page. He knows the four hands, the doctrine and where a post stands. He has heard the daylight reading whole. **He does not know that the date means anything to anybody**, the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, or what is under the bar; nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:367:**Objects and money.** **A hundred and thirty-eight marks.** The reserve sealed. **Owed: sixty yards of four-strand rope to the ferryman.** Three boxes on Brom, Lira and Cael. The kit's case with Vastin. Stake thirty-two never driven. The cord and both edges untouched by Cael since the 168th. Hesk's book has the term on the 280th's leaf and no line for the date.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:371:**Who knows what.** The mechanism: six, as before. The daylight reading: the six at the slab, and Oryn by hearing. **The date: Cael and Seln, each alone.** Nobody has interpreted the sequence, said who classed the places or why, or joined the remark to anything or anybody.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:373:**Words said aloud for the first time.** *Iron Wall* (Vastin, 16:109). The town's name, for the first time since the page (Vastin, 18:215). *Cleon* (Karis, 18:219).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:378:Movement 4 already carries day 281, six people/no mule, boxes on Brom/Lira/Cael, kit case on Vastin, the road posts, the inward reads, the station promise, and no new fragment (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,31–33,43–46`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving details:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:380:- **Paper custody:** Karis has the flat under one arm and the hide under the other; inside the flat are six counted/re-taped rows with the original technician's sheet restored to the end of row two, plus the completion report and her copy; Vastin's copied page remains in its oilcloth inside her coat; Cael laid his hand on it once, on the rise, and gave it back (coordinator ruling: the author's beat is kept) (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:141–149,155–157`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:207,271–291`). Karis also has the dead surveyor's ledger/notebook; Seln's case remains shut on his own strap (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:183–187`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:39–41`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:381:- **Knowledge:** Cael and Seln alone know that the unprinted date matches Cael's Kindling day; neither has said or written it, neither has interpreted the sequence, and neither knows for certain what the other concluded (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3–31,59–65,85–149`). Karis knows both men have read the sheet but not what they made of it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:143–149`). Vastin heard the records reading but does not know the arithmetic, integration mechanism or Cael's fragments (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`). Oryn heard the archive discussion from the basin but not the date conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:229–231`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:382:- **Bodies:** Vastin's right knee is shut, lath-bound and on day two of Oryn's thirty-day month on the 281st; stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall, and he has finally accepted being priced equally (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:151–169`). Brom's right two toes are bound with eight days left on the ten-day term, and his right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot; he must put a load down if it speaks (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:75`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:131–139`). Lira's arm remains slow and is on day sixteen out of wool (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:119–129`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:384:- **Money/objects:** purse 138; reserve sealed; sixty yards of four-strand still owed; Pike's thumbed slip is in Brom's shirt; no cordage was bought (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:149–165`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:99–101,187`). Oryn's empty bowl is Brom's to carry (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:221–223`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:386:- **Treswick/day:** it is a little before noon on day 281, at the top of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. The six have seen a bluff, river loops, three tiered walls and the pale steady station light; Cael turned his eyes to the lowest wall, and Lira has not yet performed the packet's unasked matching discipline (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:233–269`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,43`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:388:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (ch13, ch16–19; ch14–15 untouched): the eleven coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Seln on the north bank beside the factor; Cael had not known that he would say "You do now,"; Vastin names the town); no number of places and no fifth place (Karis counted groups, not places; four matched to the hide; the other sheets' corners turned down, uncounted and undescribed); the second calendar cut (Seln knew the day because he had copied that line of Cael's file twice; Cael laid the date he knows against the sheet's, a figure at a time, twice); three tracked passages re-ordered; the ruler line verbatim at the stopped lamps sentence; the remark's hand unidentified; Brom counts the spring's three findings on his fingers; the loads and the closing file made to meet Movement 4 (**Vastin took the kit case against the letter of Oryn's "you're not to" and told Cael so at once; Oryn does not know**; he walks a shoulder off Cael's left from a dozen strides down the rise). Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the settled rulings (the cut's staging, thirty-two, Oryn's past, the hand on the page) confirmed in the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch16 "Two days ago, at a board" (was three); ch18 Seln "has spent fifteen years among the seat's paper" (he copied for twelve). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 34,751 prose words (about 2% over; accepted — the added scene carries the loads and the seam); gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (16 protected). Purse 138 marks; deployment thirty-two; day 281, near noon, going down off the rise toward Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen. **There is no birthday in this book.** His own Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark; he has no Path. He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure (`the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; sealed; used exactly twice, at Ring and Stair), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used once each way), Blade (Ephram), and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). Deployment since the Line: **twenty-seven**. **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted: read three times, told to Oryn and then described to the other four, untouched since Oryn ordered him to write it down and stop touching it. His ribs have been quiet since the morning of day 129. The living purse holds 96 marks. Open accounts are listed below; `nothing owed` is false. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:23:- **The five at Lowmarch:** Lira (Wind, Iron R1 formal) has all eight left-forearm marks whole, but the arm is slung high and holds nothing until Oryn says; the right ankle is taped and unmended. She carries Oryn's crossbow, hook and one bolt and cannot span it herself. Brom (Iron Skin, Copper formal) has the right shoulder mended twice, not a third, held in four yards of webbing by the drover's turn; the older healer says it will do. Karis (Ember, **Iron Rank Three**) has 52 copied sheets (11 Ring / 29 Stair / 12 Hall), the dead surveyor's ledger, the carter's map with four circles and the line off the hide, and the Ternhall straightedge; her voice is whole and her larger hypothesis remains unspoken and unentered. Seln (Shadow, Bronze; fifteen years' service) has his **locked case**, carried shut for twelve years and unopened. Cael has Hesk's brass straightedge and satchel. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:26:- **Oryn:** last located at Thornwater, with route work north next. The old debt ran Cael→Oryn and is **PAID**: three self-readings and the full telling. Her withheld answer was never a debt. Her exact letter is: `Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.` Lira's arm waits on Oryn's in-person word. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:28:- **The Quieting:** four sites lie on one straight edge of the map. The Ring, Stair and Hall were entered. The fourth was seen and paced from outside at **440 yards and two strides** radius, behind registry-iron stake 34 repeated one per pace. It is unentered, unnamed, undated and untested; its grey central upright is unresolved and its effect unknown. `Someone made this pattern.` was said once and not answered. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:29:- **Pike/the Compact:** Pike has nine completed lines under the five names; the ninth is the Stair and reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The first-snow season line is written with no number against it. The five names remain **eleventh**. The Compact has a Fallow completion report, the Stair rim's observations and a clerk's packet saying the crew kept the kit; it does not know that fragments work inside. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4] It has reached across the Line twice: on paper (the Fallow completion report) and in person (the six on the Stair's rim). The asset-restriction is pending. **Vastin is still inside**, writing nothing, with one window in Book 7. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:30:- **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon. All six know the still-place phenomenon; only Cael and Oryn are shown hearing/saying its label. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know the fourth-site survey; Oryn, Teague and Pike do not know that result at entry. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:34:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:43:- **Count at the rim:** "Six. Six and no mule." That is Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Vastin. The word is "West."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:45:- **Cleon** stays under Treswick with the leaf and the board: "Work. Not a finding."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:54:2. **KEEP — Pike's cold-term board and the fence (140th).** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:55:3. **KEEP — The river is a road (161st); the kit on the table.** The cord is knotted at the fives, the stake is number thirty-two, plus the mallet and the field ledger with the radius line. The Stair's designation sits in an unreadable index above the stopped line "third site confirmed on bearing". Karis learns the kit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:59:7. **KEEP — Six at Lowmarch (268th).** 118 marks (the mule's shed and the rope-house roof). Karis makes her case to six: the carvings are instructions; the index; west; **Treswick and the Deepstacks named**; the scholars' provision; "a man there who is". Oryn's reservation about the station goes unsaid. **KEEP — the closing log (270th)**, verbatim (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:61:9. **KEEP — The long table (277th midday).** The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, their first words ever. The short thing: resigned or walked. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence; Vastin's new fact is "Cannot. There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail dead-ends at Treswick. Vastin has nothing to do afterwards. "Why us." Oryn on the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that can cross the Line. Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only: "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks; Vastin's close (§10). The ferry goes west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:62:10. **KEEP — The handover (277th evening)**, in Vastin's stated order. First, the records: a courier's flat of six years of survey abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), six rows, "More than four", and the completion report as the last sheet. Second, the page: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". Third, the technician's sheet: the deep-layer line and the brush bar; Karis copies it and writes "not read". Seln goes still and does not say the sum. Vastin's vertigo; Karis owns the response. Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:64:12. **KEEP — The cut (279th).** Iron Wall is first shown: a plane across the road, rooted, and therefore loud. Brom fights silent with a rock. Lira works the scree. Cael bursts away, then goes still on the scree; the pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap. Seln in the heap. Five dead and three into the sink. Costs: Brom's foot; **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson: "The wall held the line. And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." / "You do now." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:65:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (the date matches his Kindling day; "six years" is the office's survey-record rounding; no numeric span since Kindling is computed [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7]), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:66:14. **KEEP — The fork-stone (280th evening–281st first light).** Oryn's terms: "I'm not an archive person"; the city she left; "Leaving and routing are different verbs." "Three weeks" (Seln). **The promise** is written in the log and read back. She prices everyone. The Millrace rendezvous. "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." "Not the steps. Not the square." The mule goes north with her. Cael turns at a quarter-mile. Treswick comes into view from the rise; the light on the crown is not looked at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:67:15. **KEEP — The last day of the road (281st).** Lira makes the same discipline of the crown, unasked. The reading inward, a fourth and fifth time: "a cord on a stone"; the instrument is wrong for a stillness. Vastin sits; "You were the instrument. I was the error." Vastin's confession, narrowed (ruling 18): "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." Cael gives him the instrument's nothing. It is not friendship; it is ground. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:68:16. **KEEP — Treswick's outer district (282nd).** The grey bridge is older than the walls. The outer gate counts and does not ask. The mule at the trough. The inn with two doors: 136. Each of the crew looks in their own way. "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once." "They shoe by the tier." The road to the registry crosses the square, and the promise holds. Seln's report: the quarry; the provision; hands by count, up to four; the clerk; the exposure. "Four hands." / "I've two." "Entered by count. That's the door." The close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:69:17. **KEEP — Cleon at noon (283rd).** "Off floors." / "Fifty-two sheets." His terms. He stops a step late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:70:18. **KEEP — The provision (284th).** Four hands go up by count: Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin. Seln is not on the count. The square is avoided by Seln's route. The clerk does not ask and writes "four". **Lira's ladder does not pull** ("Four hands." / "Four." / "Right."). The iron door. Cleon pulls the iron to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:71:19. **KEEP — The Deepstacks (284th).** Cleon is already reading. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. "Older than [UNBOUND]." "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael is unfiled for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:72:20. **KEEP — The yard door (285th).** Vastin's reflex: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —". **Seln answers truthfully** (ruling 25; Gate 27): "He's on the count … the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was." The narration enters that Seln did not lie. "I'm sorry." / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:73:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:74:22. **KEEP — The alley (290th, dusk).** Six faceless attackers: four above with a crossbow, two below with staves, one of the four a signaller on the landing. Vastin roots the cut wall to wall ("there is no round"). Nobody declares. Brom with a rock, Lira's drop, Cael still at the plane's foot ("the reason"), Seln's weighted cord from the roof. The cache was on the roof the whole time. They leave; none taken, no faces. Costs: Karis's left hand (a step's edge), bound by Brom with thread and teeth because no healer inside the gate would touch it; Vastin spent, the knee again. **The Iron-Wall notice** (§10). "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered" / "It's entered." Not told. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:75:23. **KEEP — The reader (291st).** By the carts' street in daylight. Cleon's inside: "An instruction leans … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." **Acquisition at "there".** Cael tells Lira first ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then Cleon at the bell. "You did what." "That's not supposed to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water; **the warning**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael take the case up together. The notice on the stair. The eyes are paid on the last flight. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:76:24. **KEEP — Dividers (292nd).** Hesk's parcel and note. The meal: four marks, two cups kept for Karis and Oryn, Seln's slip read and burned ("Closed"); 130 marks. Vastin and the cups: "Out here you count who's owed a seat." The first inventory written inside walls (§12 C10). **The station's light is "not steady" for a count of one**: a pressure, "an instrument turning toward him". It becomes the fourth entry on the page. He does not cross; the promise holds at its first cost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:79:27. **KEEP — The list of parts (294th) and Cleon's goodbye at the bell:** "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:80:28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:82:30. **KEEP — The grade cracked (298th morning).** Three marks. Cleon's list puts the mark at the kindling and the mark on a sheet in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point lies past the fourth, on the line. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:85:33. **KEEP — The crest (303rd).** The watch-post: a hut, a fire, kit under a hide, a two-timber barricade, seven hoods, two crossbows, one low practitioner. "They knew." "That iron's been in the ground years. Not one cold term." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Teague: "Drawn?" "Nobody declares. Nobody dies … Noted?" / Teague's first **"Noted."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:86:34. **KEEP — The Span (304th).** First exchange: the watch's declaration is unanswered; Brom takes bolts on Iron. Teague goes through the middle (the barricade a body's length back) → **Force acquired** at a stride. Recoil: wrist, then elbow. The watch reforms. **Width:** "Nothing was gained inside" is entered first. "By count": five over stake thirty-four (Cael, Lira, Karis, the young one, Vastin), four on the shelf. They walk to the pinch. Eleven seconds. "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times." The watch goes east, unpursued. The win sentence (§10). The broad man goes over the sink's edge in the fourth second; Teague does not turn. Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers' nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's bill. **The Span** at noon: an arch on two piers over the sink, carvings on the piers' inner faces, the bearing "Through". Nothing happens on the crown. The thirteenth listens. The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:87:35. **KEEP — The shale camp (305th).** The blanket. The rows lean along the bearing. The point is fixed. **The lamps finding** (§10). Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Cael does not add his own third page (the Kindling date). **The directive and the objection**: "That's not a monolith. That's a crack." Seals unnamed. "The Compact … Yes. Part of it." The broad man's "Aye". The healers' third exchange (hands in the other's work). Seln on the pass. The fixed close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:88:36. **KEEP — The pass (306th).** Seln's reconnaissance (the shelf, the rig, nine or more, three crossbows). "It's through." The doctrine is told to Teague's four; **the young one's whole-head nod**. **The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] speaks to the six for the first time.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] The wall is set as a lean-to slant. Brom's forearm is bolted before the wall goes up. The pine and stack fall down the plane and close the mouth behind them. The scree is swept clean. Seln climbs. The broad man is hit at the slant's high edge; the young one drags him and is **killed by the sixth volley**, a stride outside the plane. Oryn's hands on him: the first time they come off with nothing done. The name is said once. [OWNER-pending #54] Seln goes over the lip at the seventh volley. **Cael's first use of Force** on the second stack's brace (stone, along the shelf); the recoil stops in the ribs. Teague takes the stair left-handed. The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] reverses her spear. The team breaks east along the ridge, none taken. Vastin goes down; Karis sits with her hand on his shoulder. Teague kneels. "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." At the far mouth Cael understands the line was not drawn in ink.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:89:37. **KEEP — The plain's edge (306th).** The burial at the east mouth by Teague's crew, with the six carrying at his leave. Lira and Seln recover the mule by the ridge path. **Eleven.** Oryn on the ribs: "Ribs. May I?" / "Yes." "That's a line. That's not yours." / "It's mine now." No term tonight. **Rune turned inward deliberately:** bones; a floor with nothing built on it; an instruction with no language; "the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's." Told to no one. The Arbiter unchanged. The instruments read wronger; the trend is up. The log (§10, "the whole year"). [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:90:38. **KEEP — The court (307th).** It lies low, and the plain is worn down to it. about 1,107 yards across (about fifty cords of the kit's twenty-stride cord) [M1 audit: 159 cords would be about 3,500 yards at Book 7's scale] [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. The stratum under everything. The first cut ("The others are copies"). The bearing ends, with no sixth. The council. **At the line:** every sigil dark at the same stride; the reactions: Lira's "Right."; Brom pricing the stump; Karis's "It's the first one."; Seln's count; Vastin's line (§10). Oryn steps in one stride: "Nothing. Everything, round it. Same as you." It is unanswered. Teague steps in one stride and steps back: "My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough … Field's mine. This isn't field." The turning begins. Lira's fixed exchange. "Wait here."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:108:| **NEW — The shale-back herd at the axe-head fence** (cold weather) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | summarized as "we walked the fence" | 3,000 | A cold-weather set piece [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] needing no Path: a herd of armoured grazers sheltering on the fence line's slope must be moved without stampeding them ("lethal on a slope when herded wrong"). It teaches the Iron read on frozen ground, Lira benched by her sling, Seln's posts, and Brom reading a line. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:109:| **NEW — The ice road** (161st) | one line | 3,000 | A carter's cart goes through the river-ice. Cael, Brom and Seln haul it out without declaring, reading load on the ice. The fragments are taught as practical knowledge. It pays later at the cut's frozen runnel. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:110:| **NEW — The silent yard** (cold-weather learning bouts with Teague's crew) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | absent | 3 bouts × ~1,500 = 4,500 | No Paths, steel and bodies only, in the frozen meadow. Cael loses to the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59]'s spear reach (she never speaks), then corrects. One-armed Lira coaches from the bench. The rival clock appears on the page. This must not touch the sequence locks in §13 (no wall drill; Seln teaches nobody). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:113:| **NEW — The tail in Treswick** (291st–292nd) | absent | 2,500 | After the alley, Seln and Cael tail a hood through the outer district at night. The hood passes through a tier gate Cael cannot legally cross. The faction stays faceless and unlocated, and the promise and the bar become physical. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:121:3. **Vastin learning the crew's doctrine and "to be nobody"** (≈5,000, distributed). Day one of the border road is a silent-movement drill: walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless meant to be loud. Then the cut's lesson, the spring's "Draft nothing", the yard door's "Be nobody", his week of moving toward the lamp and stopping (four times, then two), and the first order he takes and keeps (Millrace).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:122:4. **The Deepstacks decipherment** (≈8,000). The chamber days 285–292 are put on the page, including the undramatized 288th–289th. Cleon's method (bones before words), the board's numerals, Karis's letters coming one at a time from the three floors, and the lamp's discipline. Karis refuses to guess. **The leaf must not become readable on the page before the seventh day** (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:132:- **The 294th: the list of parts** (≈2,000). Copying all day, Cleon's finger on the last line, and his correction "Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:143:| **Brom** | Worth without a number | Prices Vastin at three hundred miles. Takes the cart's weight on the good shoulder and pays for it. Declines the broker's post by picking up the box. Says "Good" to Cleon. Carries at Teague's leave. | 10 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Seln** | To keep his old life undecided and his own | Tells only Brom about the posts. Sets the sheet before Cael without a word. Teaches Vastin the first thing he ever teaches anyone. Truthful deflection at the yard door. Walks the tiers and decides nothing. Keeps the cache "a while longer". Climbs the swept scree. | 10 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:148:| **Cleon** | The work finished and believed, without leaving the Deepstacks | Sets terms at noon. Shows the inside of the Path to no one before Karis. Refuses to finish the sentence. Looks away from the boy deliberately. Comes up the stair once. | 6 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:151:| **The young one** (Teague's; unnamed; his name is never written) [OWNER-pending #54] | To be counted as crew, not the boy with the cloth | Carries the cloth. Volunteers at the seep and is stopped. Steps over the iron when Teague looks at him ("Four"). Nods with his whole head. Goes to the broad man. | 5 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:157:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:172:| 4 | Inside Walls | 20–26 | 34,000 | S7, S8, S9 | The wrong instrument for a stillness; the enforcer's confession; the city as a machine; entered by count; the dark opens. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:173:| 5 | No Authority | 27–33 | 35,000 | S10, S11, S12 | The archive's first days; Vastin unlearning his name; Cleon's bones; Brom offered the life; the alley and the eleventh. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:195:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:196:| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:220:| 279 | The cut; **Vastin's knee (Oryn's month: day 1 = 280)**; 138 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:222:| 281 | Oryn north at first light; the rise; the last post (reading inward; confession) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:223:| 282 | Treswick outer district (136) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:224:| 283 | Cleon at noon |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:225:| 284 | The provision; the iron door |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:226:| 285 | Yard door; chamber day 2 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:227:| 286–287 | The board; Brom's yard; Seln's night walk; Cleon's close |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:234:| 294 | The list of parts; Cleon's goodbye at the bell |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:249:Running counts that must reconcile: **Lira's arm** "fifteen days" at 280, "twenty-five" at 290, "twenty-seven" at 292 and "thirty-three" at 298 (counting the 266th as day 1). **Karis's hand** is eight days old on the 298th. **Cash:** 96 → 76 → 116 → 118 → 138 → 136 → 130 → 127 → 123. **Oryn's route:** count "days past the end of her road" from the cairn on the 300th (§12 C3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:262:| **Rune Path (Cleon's)** | Taught from outside in M5 (bones), from inside in M6 (lean) | Structure, not meaning; made things only; not a river, not a man; eyes for an hour; no use in a fight | — |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:263:| **12 · Rune-adjacent** | Acquired at "there" (M6) | Eyes paid on the stair. Turned inward **unbidden** at Millrace (M7): *still*, then *set*. Turned **deliberately** at the plain's edge (M9): bones / a floor with nothing built / an instruction with no language. On the court's floor at a hundred strides: the same reading | Told to Cleon; **the inward finding told to no one** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:266:| **Tide (the tenth)** | Reading inward (M4): "a cord on a stone". Oryn's deep reading (M7). Her post-centre reading (M9) | "Ask first, every time"; Oryn's consent ritual at every reading (S18 montage, Cael at S18, S22, S24) | Same finding, certain |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:279:- Tiers and Paths in Teague's crew, in Vastin, and in Treswick's machinery (Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver; passes; tier gates; the smith's two forges; the provision's columns).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:323:- **The cut (M3).** A hundred strides of road cut to a cart's width, with scree on both sides and a frozen runnel a stride wide down the middle. A sink lies fifty-five yards below [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] on the north side, iced and in shadow; there are eight hounds. Positions: Brom on stone at the south edge with a rock; Vastin a stride behind him; Lira on the south scree; Seln on the north scree, unseen; Cael twenty strides west, past the sink; Karis, Oryn and the mule at the east end. The decisions: the wall goes up and everything turns to the loudest thing; Brom and Lira work its south end silently; Cael bursts **away**, then goes still on the scree as the lock beat lands; the pack returns to the wall and breaks on it; the heap; the runnel. The opponent learns too: the den has learned the road. Costs to carry: Brom's foot; Vastin's knee (a month); Cael's burst bill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:324:- **The alley (M5).** Twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no doors. There are four at the top (a crossbow and a signaller on the landing) and two coming up from the yard gate with staves. The plane sits at the second flight's top step, wall to wall; Cael stands two feet below it. Brom has a loose step-stone. Lira drops from the second flight. Seln's cord comes from the roof onto the signaller's arm and the rail. It lasts "a minute and some". The opponent's plan was built for a declaration and meets a wall and a rock. Costs: Karis's hand; Vastin past his limit; Brom's good shoulder used wrong.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:325:- **The Span (M8).** A shelf a cart's width wide, with the sink's three-man drop on the left and the iron on the right; the line lies a stride past the iron. A barricade of two timbers stands at the shelf's narrowest; past the fire is a pinch a stride and a half wide, then a perimeter road a pace wide. There are seven defenders: two crossbows and an empty-handed low practitioner. Exchange one belongs to the watch. Exchange two: Teague's line, with Cael at his left a stride back. Exchange three: width (five inside two strides in, four on the shelf; walk; eleven seconds). Then the fall. **Fairness is entered before the act:** nothing is gained inside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:326:- **The pass (M9).** A dry defile a hundred strides long with a loose-stone stream-bed. The west wall is scree to a shelf two-thirds up, carrying two timber-braced stacks, one with a roped dead pine; the east wall is sheer. The wall is a lean-to slant, high edge at the west wall ahead, low edge at the mouth behind. There are seven numbered volleys: Brom's forearm (1); the wall up (2); the fall (4); the broad man (5); the young one (6); Seln over the lip (7). Cael's push takes the second stack along the shelf, not off it. Teague goes up the stair left-handed; the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] reverses her spear. The team breaks along the ridge. **Win sentence:** Seln removed the team's ability to hold the high ground by climbing the slope its own rig had swept clean, and the wall bought him the climb.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:337:- **The un-bound / [UNBOUND]:** the word is live as a historical *kind* in the leaf. Before that, Karis uses it once as a stratum limit ("Older than [UNBOUND]") at Cleon's table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:339:- **The deep-layer sheet:** "Sequence initiated … Correlated with classification event —" and the bar. Only Cael and Seln do the sum. Neither says or writes it. Nobody interprets the sequence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:343:## 10. Protected wording (verbatim; canon quotes or calls back these, or Book 9 inherits them)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:350:2. **The chronicle (S15):** "— and of him it is said that he did not die in the way of men, but went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" [a thumb's width of hole]. Karis: "Marked." Cleon: "Marked."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:357:9. **Cleon's limit (S11):** "I can tell you these are orders. I can't tell you what they order. For that you need the language, and the language is in the text, not the stone. That's her work, not mine." And: "It doesn't work on a river, and it doesn't work on a man, and it doesn't work on a tree, because nobody chose where the branches went. It costs me my eyes for an hour after and nothing else."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:358:10. **Cleon's warning (S13):** "I'm going to pretend you didn't tell me that," he said, "for your sake, not mine. But I'll tell you one thing for free, since you can apparently take my whole trade by watching me work it for a minute." … "Everything I read is *made*. Stone, ink, seal — somebody built it, so I can see how. If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — " He stopped. "Don't tell me. Don't tell anyone. Just remember I said it." Chapter-close sentence: "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:359:11. **Cleon's goodbye (S17):** "Work. Not a finding." / "Mind the stair. It leans."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:361:13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:371:22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:393:- **S2 doorway:** "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. **S2 close:** "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." … "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." Also: "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." / "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." / "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:395:- **S5:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." … "Draft nothing. Just look." / "Two copies of one ignorance." Close: "Six years," Karis said. "They measured all of it. They graded it — the sites are ranked by something, and it's the same something in the kit, and I can't read either one." … "Everything I can't read points at the same place." / "Treswick," / "The archive under it. Cleon." / "Who's Cleon?" / "The only historical-Path practitioner registered west of the Line. If the language is anywhere, it's under his hands. A day and a half." … "And then I find out whether I've been right for five years or wrong for five years, and I don't know which I'm more afraid of." [OWNER-pending #52]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:396:- **S6:** "I'm not an archive person." / "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second." / "You go inside, you don't go near the station. Not the steps, not the square. You promise me in that log of yours, because I've seen what the log does to you." / the log entry: "The fork. Oryn north; five holds; routing, not the other verb. Her term, given at the fire, taken in the log because that's the form she'll take it in: inside Treswick I do not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square. Written here so she can read it, and so I can." / "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." / "Not the steps," … "Not the square."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:398:- **S8:** "Entered by count. That's the door." Close: "Last time we walked into a place like this," … "it took four years and a hearing to walk out." [OWNER-pending #53] / "Last time we didn't know what we were looking for." / "Do we now?" / "A name and a reason," … "Older than the walls, under our feet, and nobody's read it because nobody's had a reason to look and a person who could read it in the same lifetime." … "That's us. That's the whole reason it's still buried. We're the first ones who are both." (On "four years" see §12 C2: this is the one place where Cael's spoken rounding stands.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:399:- **S9:** "Off floors," / "Fifty-two sheets." / "Four hands," / "Four." / "Right." / the log: "Lira looked at the whole ladder from the top of it and it didn't pull. She priced it. She's carrying a box."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:400:- **S10:** "Older than [UNBOUND]," / "I know that hand." / "Being believed — " … "It's the end of being able to be wrong." / "Give me a week." / "I'm sorry," / "Don't be sorry," Seln said. "Be nobody." Log: "Karis has been looking for this room her whole life. Cleon's been sitting in it for thirty years waiting for her. Vastin tried to open a door with his rank and nearly closed all of them — an Archmarshal's worth nothing here, which he's taking about as well as I took [SHATTERED]. Down here the stone's older than the Compact, so the Compact doesn't reach. First place inside walls I've ever stood where nobody can file me, and it's a hole under a city, and it's because everything down here is older than the machine that files. Karis says give her a week. I've got a box to carry and a promise to keep about a station upstairs. I can wait."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:401:- **S11 close:** "You've been reading the strata. Old, older, oldest — I know, I read your face, you've dated these past anything the Compact admits." … "Here's what the strata can't tell you. These aren't the ruins of something. This is the *documentation* of something. Somebody wrote these down so the thing could be *built the same way twice*." … "In thirty years I never had the stone to match the text. You walked in with three floors." … "I don't think you're going to like what you've found, Karis. I've had a piece of it for a decade and I've never once slept well since." Also: "You think Karis is right? That it's all built on something?" / "I think we're about to find out." / "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." / Seln: "I looked at it." / log: "Brom was offered the life. He picked up the box." / "Seln looked at it. Decided nothing."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:404:- **S14 log lines:** "Hesk sent dividers. Lines are for finding out how far a thing is from another thing. Everything is. I'll enter that as a rule and see what it's worth." / "The promise stands. Not the steps. Not the square." Also: "Out here you count who's owed a seat," … "It's a different ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:406:- **S19:** "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / "Noted," / "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times," / win sentence: "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." / Teague's arm: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that now," Log body: "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth. Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend. The Span's the fourth site and the Compact fenced it, years ago by the scale on the iron, and left men on it. They knew. They've always known. The bearing runs through it and keeps going, oldest-last, and the oldest one's out there in the deep edge, quiet since they built the machine. One more site. I've wanted to stand in the middle of it since Karis said *someone made this.* Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:409:- **S22 log body:** "Turned the Rune fragment on myself. Cleon said don't. The reading only ever told me the still place was nothing — no flow, no current, a hole where a man should have a middle. The Rune sense says it's not a hole. It says it's *built like something* — like one of those floors with nothing standing on it. Same shape to that fragment as the sites are to Cleon's. I'm not going to write what that might mean, because I don't know, and because the last time I wrote something true in this log a healer made me swear an oath about it. The instruments read wronger for me than they did at Lowmarch. The trend's climbing. My Arbiter's still dark—nothing in me to go quiet, same as always. Tomorrow, the oldest one. I've spent the whole year wanting to stand in the middle of it. I think part of me already knows what I'm going to feel. Nothing. I think I'm going to feel nothing, and I think that's going to be the loudest thing that's ever happened to me." [OWNER-pending #58] ("the whole year", never "the whole book".) [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:432:| Seln's Book 12 choice | 12 | No foreshadow beyond the cache kept undecided. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:439:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:442:- **C5 — Rune's tier.** The universe bible says "Cael's twelfth (Rune-adjacent, partial, Bronze)". The notice says "Rune family … Tier equivalent unknown". **Edition follows the notice.** Bronze is Cleon's tier.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:447:- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:450:- **C13 — Reader Standard repairs already made in the source.** Seln does not lie at the yard door (ruling 25). Consent is asked before every reading (S18 montage and Cael, S22, S24). **The edition carries both and adds no exception.** The source has no profanity and no gore to remove.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:460:- **Cael lies still for no one but Oryn,** and she has read him three times (sack, table, marsh's edge) until Millrace. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling — in the edition's Book 7 Oryn's hands were on Cael for several surface reads that found nothing (the mountain; the ford at Oxhollow; the stake), for the long reading on the 100th (the table), and at the Hall on the 120th (the marsh's edge); Cael has read Oryn twice, each time after asking and an explicit yes.] **Oryn does not read Cael** before Millrace's deep reading; she reads his ribs' surface at most.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:461:- **Seln teaches nobody anything** before "Draft nothing. Just look." (280th, to Vastin).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:462:- **Seln and Vastin exchange no words** before the 277th long-table doorway.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:467:- **Vastin** takes no order without walking it back before Millrace's "Stand there". He does not sit in front of the crew between the cut and the road's last post (281st).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:468:- **Cleon** is above ground with the crew only once (the yard fire). Otherwise he is at noon at his tavern, or on the stair. He takes no notice of Cael until he is told.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:470:- **The mule** goes north with Oryn on the 281st and returns at Millrace on the 298th. From the fork to Millrace the boxes are carried on backs (ruling 16).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:471:- **The square and the station steps:** Cael never sets foot on them. He never looks at the crown except at the count-of-one.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:472:- **Cleon's name** is first heard by Cael on the 280th. **Treswick and the Deepstacks** are first spoken aloud at the 268th table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:473:- **Karis cannot read the index as a grade** until the 298th. The leaf is not readable on the page before the seventh day of Cleon's week.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:482:**Names pending owner approval: none required.** Every new figure the expansion needs is carried by role: the axe-head hold's factor, the carter at the ice road, the ferryman and his boy, Oryn's route patients (at Oxhollow and unnamed holds), the hold child at the Kindling, the broker's men, and the hood in the tail. This keeps the audio load low in a book whose cast is already heavy with role-names (Teague's crew must stay unnamed by canon). If the author finds a recurring role that needs a name in the audio, it is listed here for approval before drafting, and drafted under the proposed name per the edition's policy (RUN-LEDGER 18:41).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:484:**Existing names stay exactly as canon has them.** Never "Halcenvane" on the page; use "the academy above Ostrand". The registry collisions are untouched (OWNER-DECISIONS #6). **Audiobook read-through list** (carried): Cleon/Cael (KLEE-on/KAYL; never in one spoken run); Span/Stair; Treswick/Ternhall (keep them out of one spoken inventory); the O-onset stack Oryn/Oxhollow/Ostrand; Pike/Fiske. Places minted by canon only: Treswick, the Deepstacks, the Sunken Span, "the court" (description), the shoulder hold, the cut, the pass. **Do not name new holds** on Oryn's route. Use Oxhollow or Thornwater, or none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:490:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three future holds and "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."; Teague's "After the next thaw" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael remains nineteen at the Book 9 opening. Do not place or calculate his next birthday until the owner rules the series calendar. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**

