   306	- **The fork (the 280th evening; the 281st).** Oryn: "I'm not an archive person."; her past (a house for the sick in a city inside the Line; the column for the patient's tier; a woman from the river sheds whom she mended off the sheet; she walked out of a gate and has not been through one since — the author's, kept); "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second."; Seln's "Three weeks"; **the station term, written in the log and read back (verbatim)**; she priced all six, Vastin as long as the rest; "That's on me. It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." (the reading she has not given Cael); "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it."; "Not the steps," … "Not the square." She went north with the brown mule, her linen and the crossbow with its one bolt: five gates, the ford, Millrace in three weeks.
