   186	
   187	It was the first time that he had been all the way round.
   188	
   189	He lay and counted what he had, and it was a good deal. He knew where the place was. He knew how far out the leaning began, for each of the nine. He knew that the way round was worn smooth, with never a ripple in it; and he knew now how far it was about. He went down that column with something like pride, as a small pale woman went down a row that agreed.
   190	
   191	Then he saw what kind of column it was.
   192	
   193	Every line of it was about a thing that moved. It told him where the Wind leaned, and how the millstone went by. There was not one line in it about the place. There never had been. *Doesn't flow. Doesn't change.* He had written those on a leaf, and had taken them for findings about the place; and they were not. They were only the instrument's way of saying where it left off.
