     5	## Standing facts carried in
     6	
     7	- A little before noon on the 281st, going down the west side of the long rise. Six and no mule. File: Seln thirty yards ahead with empty hands; Lira with the second box on her back, both arms through its beckets; Brom with the heaviest on his left shoulder; Karis with the flat under one arm and the hide under the other, and the copied page in oilcloth inside her coat; Cael with the third box; Vastin a shoulder off on Cael's left, ditch side, the tarred kit case slung above his sound leg. Brom has the purse, Pike's thumbed slip and Oryn's empty bowl.
     8	- Purse 138 marks. Reserve sealed in the third box. Sixty yards of four-strand owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
     9	- Ten fragments. Deployment since the Line thirty-two. Shadow twice and sealed; Anchor's counted uses two; Tide on Oryn twice, on himself three times, on nobody else. The still place read three times and untouched since Oryn's order.
    10	- Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it. One registry reckoning; no figures; no span.
    11	- Karis matched four sign-groups to the hide and gave no number of places. The remark's hand is not identified.
    12	- Vastin: right knee lath-bound, the 281st being the second day of thirty (twenty-eight after it); stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall. He has not sat in front of the crew since the cut. No age. He does not know the mechanism, what Cael carries, or the sum.
    13	- Brom: two toes of the right foot, eight days left on the 281st; the right shoulder in the older healer's knot. Lira: arm on its sixteenth day out of the wool; slow; not to be fallen on.
    14	- Oryn: north of the fork with the brown mule, her linen, the crossbow and one bolt. Five gates, the ford, Millrace in three weeks. She owes Cael the reading. Her past as told: a house for the sick inside a wall; the column for the patient's tier; a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; not through a gate since.
    15	- The term in the log: inside Treswick Cael does not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square.
