   185	## Changes made while drafting (written after the draft)
   186	
   187	- **Chapter 20 has six scenes.** The first was divided at the nine-mile post. In scene 4 the stone under his hand is the field gate's hanging-post, of the same dressed stone as the mile-mark, since he read himself behind the hedge and not at the post.
   188	- **Chapter 21.** Brom lights the fire with flint and steel: Karis keeps her point shut on a town's ground, three miles from a gate, and Seln says why. The fifth reading is made sitting against the three-mile post and does not go round a second time. Vastin's own sentence from an inquiry ("The instrument is not at fault. It has told you where its reach ends.") comes back to him from Cael, who never saw the paper it stands in (Book 6 ch14, ch40).
   189	- **Chapter 22.** The rope is priced and no figure is printed (the book's cash track leaves three marks between the 292nd and the 298th, and I did not wish to fix a price that a later movement must meet).
   190	- **Chapter 23 has six scenes.** Seln's report is given in two sittings, with the lantern burned down a finger's breadth between the four things and the difficulty. He did not go above the trough: he hired a frame for a copper and sat three hours on the porters' bench. Vastin's papers are "three sheets under one seal", in oilskin, beside Karis's receipt.
   191	- **Chapter 24.** Seln goes up alone on the 283rd as a counted hand (a keg of lamp oil, on a buff card) to walk both ways to the yard; Lira stays in the loft, so that the 284th is her first sight of the town from its top. Nobody says that evening who is to carry.
   192	- **Chapter 25.** Oryn reaches the second gate after dark on the third day; the bed is in a gate-house built on the wall's outer face, so that she goes through no gate. The matter card is rare enough that both upper keepers remark on it (neither asks anything).
   193	- **Chapter 26.** On the cut's fourth flight the stick slips; Compression comes up into Cael's heels unasked and is told to wait; the load does not come. Not a use. The registry's lowest three courses, and the undercroft beyond the last pillar, are of the bridge's dark dry-laid stone. Cleon's name is on the page once, in the last scene, and nowhere in chapter 24.
   194	- **Fragments, as written:** the read asked at the nine-mile post and on the bridge (told that it need not know). Anchor asked at the outer gate's sill, at the second gate twice, at the third gate and at the iron sill (told no each time). Shadow lifted at dusk on the 281st and the 283rd (told no). Compression rose on the stair (told to wait). Tide on himself, twice, on the 281st (not counted). Nothing was used outward. Deployment thirty-two.
