editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md:51:"Mine," she said. "The keeper of the archive at Ternhall wrote to me this morning, privately. Four lines. A district clerk came to her counter six days ago with a sealed request for my transfer file: my old standing, my privileges, the training log from the paired floor." She kept two fingers on the letter, as if it might blow away. "On the Third-day a fee office wanted to know who I was. Now somebody wants to know who I used to be." She was quiet a moment. "That's twice."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md:69:Brom had come up behind them, slower. At the turn of the stair he stopped, and Cael, a step below, saw his right hand go to the left side of his coat, where the inside pocket was, and rest there over the cloth. There was a square cream envelope in that pocket with its dark red seal still whole. It had come up with the post four days ago, and he had turned it over once at the table and put it away unopened, and nobody had asked. Now an office in his own province kept an open book with a question in it about his family, and his grandmother could turn its pages whenever she liked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-58.md:5:The district officer's envelope came back to the seat at Ostrand on the Seventh-day evening, by his own hand, opened and endorsed. *No such enrollee; withdrawn this day; see the registrar's certificate.* The certificate followed in the house's bag on the First-day morning, with four leaves of the registry's own form under the house's seal, and one of the four had three lines of longhand in its margin.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:213:"I have made something over nine thousand evaluations," said Vastin, to the case, very quietly. "I counted them once, as a young man, and stopped counting when I stopped being one. Each of them I wrote down exactly as I found it, and sent up." His left hand opened on his knee and closed. "How many went into the registry as I wrote them, I don't know. I never shall. That is what I am taking home from this room. Not the paper. That."
