+   new: `"I wrote *declined*, and I gave a reason, which was a true one, and I have been thought the better of for it by six people on a moor." He shut his eyes. "I did not decline only to spare you a plate. I declined because the office had shown me what it did with honest readings; and part of me was relieved that I need never learn what the plate would say. I kept my hand off a door for a sound reason, and I was glad of it for a bad one. That is what I have carried from the seat to this bank, and it is not in the flat."`
